{
  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far shows that multiprofile + transformer aggregation + weighted fusion with scvi_n200 and imagenet_vit_l achieves the best performance (config_025: 0.725 acc / 0.685 F1), and that multiprofile is the dominant design lever (~0.18 gain over singleprofile). However, the RNA encoder choice is the largest untested dimension—we have only ever used scvi_n200. Config_019 is a clean single-variable swap (scvi_n200 → pca_n2000) within the best-performing multiprofile/transformer/weighted/imagenet_vit_l setup. This directly tests whether a learned RNA representation (scvi) adds meaningful value over a simple linear one (PCA-2000) in the regime where the model is already strong. If pca_n2000 matches scvi_n200, it tells us the RNA encoder is not a bottleneck and we can redirect budget toward image encoder or fusion; if it degrades substantially, it confirms the learned encoder's importance and justifies further investment in scgpt or other learned encoders. This is the highest-information-per-experiment choice because it isolates one critical, completely unexplored variable in the most promising configuration."
}

